<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Here's the honest answer first. We checked the Perth market and found no engineering firm that publishes a fee for an engineer's crack report, beam design for wall removal, a site-specific patio or shed certificate, extension or footing design, or an hourly rate. Engineers quote each job, and the price depends on the house, the structure and what the council needs. Anyone showing you a neat Perth price table for engineering is quoting estimates, not published fees.</p><p>What we can give you is the list of things that move a quote up or down, the Perth figures that do exist (mostly building-inspection products, labelled as such), and the permit fees and levies set by regulation. Kings Park Structural Co is advertising, not an engineering firm. We pass your enquiry to the independent structural engineering firm that advertises here, and it quotes you and contracts with you directly. Send photos or plans and the engineer who quotes your job can tell you what it needs, starting with <a href="/structural-inspections/">structural inspections</a> if a crack is what's keeping you up.</p></div></div></section>
